/T (Key Terms What is CCS \(Charge Sheeted Cases\) ? CCS \(Cases Charge Sheeted\) refers to the number of cases in which the police have completed their investigation and filed a charge sheet in court. This indicates that the investigation found enough evidence to formally accuse someone of the crime. In simple terms: These are cases where the police believe the accused should face trial.)
